# Code owners for agentic-handbook (the adopter template).
#
# WHAT THIS DOES AND DOES NOT DO — stated plainly, because a CODEOWNERS file people believe is
# enforcing when it is not is worse than no file at all.
#
# GitHub only *requires* code-owner review when the branch protection rule for `main` sets
# `require_code_owner_review: true`. It is currently FALSE here: this repository runs a
# solo-operator model, and requiring a code-owner review would mean requiring a second person who
# does not exist — the merge would be unsatisfiable rather than protected.
#
# So today it requests the owner as a reviewer automatically, records which paths are privileged
# surface, and becomes ENFORCING with no further edit the day a second maintainer exists.
#
# Recorded as a Tier-A precondition at the 2026-07-27 floor-#3 review ("CODEOWNERS on .github/").

